# Normalise all text files to LF inside the repo regardless of which
# OS the developer is on. Without this, a Windows checkout with
# `core.autocrlf=true` will convert LF → CRLF on read and back again
# on write — but if either side gets it wrong, `git status` shows
# dozens of files as "modified" with ZERO content diff and commits
# end up flip-flopping between line-ending styles.
#
# `text=auto` lets git auto-detect text vs binary; `eol=lf` forces
# the in-repo (and checked-out) representation to be LF on every
# platform. Editors on Windows handle LF files just fine today.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly mark common binary types so git never tries to do
# line-ending or diff text shenanigans on them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tar binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.wav binary
